5 69 13 80 90","","","a","The museum is the old, catacomb like, water cisterns under Søndermarken park opposite the main entrance to Zoo, and the unusual environs, combined with the stained glass art and various sculptures makes the museum quite unique."],["Det Kinesiske Lysthus","attraction",55.67555,12.52752,"","","","","","a"],["Galleri Niels Træsborg","antiques",55.67662,12.52042,"","Fr 12:00-17:30","","","","s"],["Vesten for Humlen","park",55.66708,12.53703,"","","","","","a"],["Frederiksberg Slot","castle",55.67183,12.52527,"","","","","","a"],["Zoologisk Have København","zoo",55.67205,12.52133,"","Jan-Mar 10:00-16:00; Apr-May: 09:00-17:00; Jun: 09:00-18:00; Jul-Aug 10: 09:00-20:00; Aug 11-Sep: 09:00-18:00; Oct: 09:00-17:00; Nov-Dec: 10:00-16:00; Dec 24: 1","+45 72 200 200","","","a"],["Digterlunden","park",55.67636,12.53217,"","","","","","a"],["City Hall (Rådhuset)","sight",55.67863,12.53142,"Smallegade 1-3","Tours the first Sat each month at 13:00","","","","r","The massive city hall took 10 years to complete, because the city council failed to see World War II coming, and war time turned out not to be the best period getting materials. The somewhat oversize building might be a result of…"],["Storm P. Museum","sight",55.67478,12.53186,"Frederiksberg Runddel","","","","","r","Robert Storm Petersen (Storm P) was a famous Danish artist and author, his humorous works is often regarded as something quintessentially Danish. The museum owns more than 50,000 drawings (of which only some are on exhibition). Storm P…"],["Revymuseet","sight",55.6754,12.53169,"Allégade 5","Tue-Sun 11:00-16:00","","","","r","Revue theatre is still a very popular art form in Denmark, underpinned by the Danes love of black (or dry) humour. And since Frederiksberg has played an important role in the history of Danish theatre, it is only natural that you find a…"],["The Bakkehus Museum","sight",55.66844,12.53205,"Rahbeks Allé 23","Tue-Sun 11:00-16:00","","","","r","Recommended by Wikivoyage"],["Frederiksberg Palace","sight",55.67139,12.52511,"Roskildevej 28","Tours the first Saturdays of each month at 11:00 and 13:00","","","","r","The baroque palace dates back to 1699 and used to be a royal residence, today it functions as home of the Royal Danish Army Officers Academy. It can be viewed from the gardens or on the monthly tours."],["Copenhagen Zoo","sight",55.67169,12.52327,"Roskildevej 32","Opening hours varies greatly throughout the season, but Mon-Fri 09:00-16:00 & Sat Sun 09:00-18:00 are always safe bets. During high season daily: 09:00-21:00","","","","r","The Copenhagen Zoo is one of the oldest in Europe tracing its history back to 1859. Its focus has shifted from displaying as many animals as possible, to providing large, world class facilities to the animals, earning the zoo a…"],["The Betty Nansen Theater","activity",55.67405,12.537,"Frederiksberg Allé 57","Office: Mon-Fri 14:00-18:00, Sat 14:00-16:00","","","","r","A good, popular and long-running local theatre, back from the heydays of Frederiksberg theatre, but English performances are rare, so it is best suited for Scandinavian speakers."],["Camp X Theatre","activity",55.67867,12.53299,"Smallegade 2 & Frederiksberg Allé 102","Office: Mon-Fri 14:00-18:00, Sat 14:00-16:00","","","","r","A modern, lightly experimental, theatre on Frederiksberg where English or other international performances, or visitors, are not unusual."],["Cafe Sokkelund","restaurant",55.67909,12.52636,"Smallegade 36","Mon-Thu Sat 10:00-23:00, Fri 10:00-00:00, Sun 10:00-21:00","","","","r","Brasserie-style French cafe, whose 100-kroner brunch is a good deal, and the premier draw at this place. Anything else is fine and OK, but nothing you'll remember the minute you walk out of there."],["Hansens Old Family Garden","restaurant",55.67278,12.53141,"Pile Alle 10-12","All year 11:00-00:00","","","","r","The oldest of the Frederiksberg garden restaurants. The main building is from 1630. Serves very traditional Danish food in mix between a Garden and an outdoor German style Beer hale, but also has indoor seating. No music played"],["Kartellet","restaurant",55.67573,12.53304,"Allégade 8A","Mon-Thu 10:30-22:00, Fri Sat 10:00-00:00, Sun 10:00-21:00","","","","r","Located in one of the old houses along Allégade, with outdoor seating in small garden facing the street, and indoor seating in tasteful large room. A good brunch menu (130 kr), Café lunch (burgers, sandwiches, etc.) and a small,…"],["Krøgers Family Garden","restaurant",55.67116,12.53064,"Pile Alle 18","only during summer (May-Sep)","","","","r","Only dating back to 1864, this is the youngest of the family gardens, where you sit outside on long benches drinking beer while garbling in traditional Danish fare. Live music every weekend in the summer"],["Café Intime","bar",55.67722,12.5322,"Allégade 25","Daily 18:00-02:00","","","","r","A really cosy, and as the name suggests; intimate bar, with candle light, coloured lamps and purposely messy decoration. Frequent live Jazz and Classic music acts, which also turns really intimate as there isn't a lot of space, after a…"],["Cafe Kellerdirk","bar",55.67498,12.53318,"Frederiksberg Allé 102","Mon-Thu 11:00-00:00, Fri Sat 11:00-05","","","","r","Named after two of the biggest names in Danish theatre, this place has a history going back nearly 200 years, though the current buildings has been converted from a theatre build in 1919. Salsa night every Monday (and Salsa courses the…"],["Carlsberg Visitors Centre","sight",55.66555,12.52832,"Gamle Carlsberg Vej 11","Tue-Sun 10:00-16:00","","","","r","While Denmark's largest and most famous beer producer has moved production from this historic location, to a modern facility in the provinces, it is still possible to visit the old brewery, and small scale production of speciality beers…"]]}